{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds","id":815913,"title":"[Sell me on] The Bale Hounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-24T23:06:18-08:00","id":815913,"title":"[Sell me on] The Bale Hounds","content":"What's this? Doesn't Bunyip already know this game? Has the world gone mad? Cats and dogs living together in peace and harmony aaaarghhhh!!<br /> <br /> Ahem. Sorry, back to being serious. <br /> <br /> A lot of people really like the Bale Hounds. Some like them more than that (wyrdhamster, I'm looking at you). <br /> <br /> Various recent threads have had people saying how much they're looking forward to 2E Bale Hounds, and I'm curious to better understand this. <br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm a fan of both flavours of Werewolf - you don't need to sell me on that. But, I've never seen Bale Hounds as that interesting. With Pure and Claimed and Spirits and other Forsaken and everything else in the CofD my werewolves have had enough on their plate without me spending too much time thinking about Bale Hounds. <br /> <br /> But 2E is here, and now I'm thinking different flavours of werewolves. I'm thinking Pure, I'm thinking other things. <br /> <br /> What interests you about Bale Hounds? What do you like/love? What do you think they should look like in 2E?<br /> <br /> I know you're out there. Sell me on them. <br /> <br /> Caveat: This shouldn't in any way be interpreted as Bale Hounds being on the current writing calendar. I just think about 'what next?' for both Forsaken and Apocalypse probably more than I should <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:52:19-08:00","id":815932,"title":"","content":"I think the most interesting aspect of the Bale Hounds is the paranoia they can create.<br /> <br /> The Pure are nuanced ideological antagonists, but they're not really good for subverting the PC's views. They proselytize too overtly, even if some of them can do so with amazing skill at making the Uratha question their allegiances. You're never going to find out you've being targeted for conversion to the Pure after it is too late to turn back.<br /> <br /> The other antagonists in the game aren't really going to even try for this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds though, can really run a long game on the Uratha and slowly draw them in without outing themselves. You can never 100% know if one's trying to convert you, or something else, in service of their master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T00:43:00-08:00","id":815943,"title":"","content":"I like them as an opponent that unify Forsaken and Pure.<br /> I like them as explorations of how Forsaken view embodiments of human &quot;sin&quot; in werewolf form.<br /> I like them as corrupting influences and &quot;the enemy within&quot; hook.<br /> I like them as agents of non techgnostic &quot;demons&quot;.<br /> I liked the presentation options of individual, lodge and 9th Tribe. The 9th Tribe option was my preferred option.<br /> <br /> As an ST I like having non PC splats to work with, the Pure aren't that anymore. I'm a fan of the Maeljin and want to see them developed into something substantial, even if they are a holdover from Apocalypse they aren't the same beings in CoD. I'd like to see them get their own Blue Book treatment that is more substantive than what they got in Inferno that can be used across multiple game lines. I'd be happy if they were part of the reason for the existence of the God Machine and it's angels, one of it's functions being that it helps keep them from infecting the system. That doesn't even have to be the reason the GM exists, just a fortunate side effect of its existence. Don't need stats, these are entities no pack is going to beat down or hunt to destruction, but I'd like to see motivations and methods explored, in relation to the larger CoD universe. They aren't defeated by direct confrontation but by countering their schemes, ala Lovecraft's Mythos entities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T01:12:38-08:00","id":815950,"title":"","content":"I want to get back to this, but I don't have time right now and I'd need to reread some stuff on Bale Hounds. For the moment, I leave you with one of those comparisons they teach you how to do on the SATs:<br /> <br /> Forsaken:Pure:Bale Hounds::Pentacle:Seers:Scelesti. Or maybe you'd prefer Traditions:Technocracy:Nephandi.<br /> <br /> The Pure are focused on their, well, purity. They are werewolves among werewolves that seek to avenge Father Wolf and bring back a primeval global Hunting Ground. They are the extremes of both the savagery of Flesh and and weirdness of Spirit, and their ideology borders on alien in a very distinctly spirtual way. Even the ones who are slaves serve the great spirits of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds are the Other. They seek out and serve things that by all rights either should not exist in the Shadow or make the shadow infinitely worse. They're corruptive, and insidious, and somewhat alien in a truly non-werewolf way. In a way, they were the original out-of-context problem that the Uratha have to deal with.<br /> <br /> The human version would be...think about the horror that comes with coming face to face with a full-on neo Nazi skinhead. You probably disagree fundamentally with their ideology, and in some ways they embody the worst of being human...but they <i>are</i> human. It's like looking in a mirror. Contrast that with looking at something that's at least somewhat fundamentally <i>other</i> that you can't understand, something intent on spreading that inhumanity. The Bale Hounds are the werewolf version of that.<br /> <br /> Or to paraphrase a discussion from Exalted, the Forsaken and the Pure are two sides of the same coin. Bale Hounds are paper money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T01:26:19-08:00","id":815952,"title":"","content":"Good thoughts so far, thanks. <br /> <br /> To add another wrinkle to this discussion, what do Bale Hounds add that Idigam don't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T01:42:59-08:00","id":815956,"title":"","content":"Well, as an addition to what I said, what the Bale Wolves add is a similarity to the People that the Idigam can't match - they are still the Other, but more importantly they're the Self -corrupted- by the Other. For yet -another- comparison to a different gameline, it's like how Belial's Brood and the Strix have a lot of thematic overlap but ultimately deliver significantly different experiences.<br /> <br /> Also it might just be me but I see Idigam as a Big Deal(tm) to add to a campaign, something that necessitates a level of narrative focus that I sometimes don't necessarily want in my game. Bale Hounds are more subtle, both kinda uniform and more diverse IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T01:46:42-08:00","id":815959,"title":"","content":"That... doesn't entirely seem like a fair comparison. It seems like it would be more useful to consider what the Maeljin add that the Idigam don't.<br /> <br /> For me, the Maeljin add familiarity. For all their horrors, they represent emotional concepts we know from instinct and experience. You can understand (even if you don't condone) how someone might get caught up with an entity of destructive lust. <br /> <br /> The Idigam represent the unknowable. They're terrifying because what you think you recognize as patterns or methods in them are are protean and slippery. Defeating them isn't simply difficult because of their immense power, but because they are alien to the already alien spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T02:37:19-08:00","id":815974,"title":"","content":"So I'm actually not wild on the Bale Hounds myself, so I might struggle to sell them. I can offer one huge benefit that I see to them though and see if that helps.<br /> <br /> Because they're the enemy it's easy for the Forsaken to start thinking that the Pure are simply evil. Having a group out there that deliberately embraces vice and holds such a twisted code of values helps to show the difference between antagonists and villains. I think it gives a clearer impression of the Pure to have other werewolves out there like the Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:04:12-08:00","id":816075,"title":"","content":"Let me add my two cents:<br /> <br /> For me, Bale Hounds are the true antagonists of Werewolf The Forsaken. I will try to explain how they fit in my stories by comparing them to the struggles a mortal human might face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagine you are a farmer that lives with your family, all of you isolated somewhere in the mountains. You have animals and vegetables, both helping you sustain your family. Wild beasts sometimes kill your live stock, and you have to deal with them. Insects destroy your crops, and you apply pest control.<br /> <br /> There is another family whose farm borders yours. Sometimes you help them, sometimes they help you, they are OK neighbors and you trust them to a degree.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the mountain, there is another family of farmers, one that has been hating you for generations because your grand grand father had feud with theirs. Your relationship with them is tense at best, and you advise your children to stay away from their land.<br /> <br /> And, every now and then, really bad weather hits your land, leaving a trail of chaotic destruction that you need to repair and prepare for if you want to survive.<br /> <br /> One night, you find a lone stranger near-dead by the river. You help and nurse him, treating him like family, and after sometime everyone loves him. You feel joy when your daughter announces their marriage, and you help him build another wooden-house near yours. Time passes, they have children, and he ends up leading the family as you grow old and tired. You feel safer now, you think everything is gona be OK. Until one day he convinces you to go for a weekend of fishing, and as drowns you, he tells you that he will sell your entire land to a mining company, that he has done the same to all your neighbors, and your family will think that it was what you wanted. </div> </div> </div>In this scenario, the Family is your pack, the farm is your territory, animals are the humans living there, and plants are the spirits. Wild beasts are the ocasional humans that go out of control, and insects are spirits that need to be erradicated and pest control is the change in ressonance. The first neighbors are another Forsaken pack, and the other family are the Pure that hate you. The bad weather are the Indigam, forces of nature that you cannont predict realiably and most of the time can only repair the damage caused. Well, the Bale Hound is the last guy...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=815952#post815952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thoughts so far, thanks.<br /> <br /> To add another wrinkle to this discussion, what do Bale Hounds add that Idigam don't?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I successfuly managed to comunicate my feelings about the Bale Hounds above, but to sum up: An Indigam is something like the Moby-Dick, while the Bale Hound is 006 from Goldeneye, the guy you though was your friend but in fact was behind everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 01-25-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:36:19-08:00","id":816092,"title":"","content":"I remember hearing part of the 2e team (I want to say Stew, but even so it was all imaginative musing) once say they'd like to make a book on them that would explore the Maeljin as Inferno demons, Shadow spirits of evil, or 'something else.'<br /> <br /> Of course, 'something else' is always evocative, for being vague. I guess that's what the Idigam are in a way, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:39:40-08:00","id":816094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816075#post816075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me add my two cents:<br /> <br /> For me, Bale Hounds are the true antagonists of Werewolf The Forsaken. I will try to explain how they fit in my stories by comparing them to the struggles a mortal human might face.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In this scenario, the Family is your pack, the farm is your territory, animals are the humans living there, and plants are the spirits. Wild beasts are the ocasional humans that go out of control, and insects are spirits that need to be erradicated and pest control is the change in ressonance. The first neighbors are another Forsaken pack, and the other family are the Pure that hate you. The bad weather are the Indigam, forces of nature that you cannont predict realiably and most of the time can only repair the damage caused. Well, the Bale Hound is the last guy...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know if I successfuly managed to comunicate my feelings about the Bale Hounds above, but to sum up: An Indigam is something like the Moby-Dick, while the Bale Hound is 006 from Goldeneye, the guy you though was your friend but in fact was behind everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm sold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T07:55:19-08:00","id":816107,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: WtF is not one of my primary gameline loves, so consider what I say from that perspective.<br /> <br /> I have an unhealthy fondness for the concepts of Temptation and agents of Corruption. As others have said, a Pure is almost always going to be obvious to you and the servants of the Idigam often too alien. But your best friend could be a Bale Hound and you would not know it. He listens, he usually gives good advice. And maybe one day you are in a serious bind but he has &quot;friends&quot;, powerful ones that can help you, if you but do one tiny, itty favour for them. And why not? The Pure are ideological enemies and the Idigam are bizarre, but Bale Hounds and the things they serve just want you to give in. To take what you really want, -Nay!- <i>deserve</i>! Why bother with all this crap when you know things are not really going to get better? Just take a trip to a Wound to see how fucked everything is.<br /> <br /> Some other quick points (many have already been raised):<ul><li>They give a quick and easy reason for Forsaken and Pure to work together without involving the Strange and Bizarre</li> <li>They allow for introduction of werewolves with powers that are outside the general wheelhouse of regular Gifts, presenting surprising challenges while keeping it in a werewolf package</li> <li>They expand the mythology in interesting ways</li> </ul><br /> Lastly, from a more holistic viewpoint, they make the Chronicles of Darkness seem more coherent. Demonic entities are a thing all shadow-kin encounter and it is not just vampires who can align with them (i.e. Belial's Brood) or mages who make pacts with them. Werewolves too can form major groups around a common setting element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:21:17-08:00","id":816122,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about Bale Hounds - they almost <i>require</i> the presence of Wounds and the Maeljin. The maeljin and wounds, much like the entire Inferno thing, seem to have gained less importance as Virtues / Vices changed from being the objective good/evil vibes, and now represent other things. Yes, comparisons to Belial's Brood, Scelesti, and Loyalists stand out. These are the werewolves who've sold themselves to &quot;demons&quot; and other beings of incredible evil. In many ways, they're the new Black Spiral Dancers. But they're kind of limited, again by that whole Wound thing. Wounds are pretty much almost restricted, by nature, to cities as well.<br /> <br /> Wait, you say. This is supposed to be a thread about SELLING the Bale Hounds. Not bashing them. Go somewhere else, you hater. <br /> <br /> But wait, I say. I'm just setting the stage. I have yet begun to sell. Ahem. Now, lets get into the meat of the matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wounds are pretty much the Infernally tainted areas of the Hisil. And, with all things Inferno, we're looking at the embodiments of human foils and failings. Think about that for a moment. The Pure represent werewolves who want to exalt the Shadow over the Flesh. The Forsaken want to balance the worlds. The Bale Hounds... want to exalt the Flesh over the Shadow. They're the embodiment human antipathy to the world around them, seeing it as a wasted thing only good for living in it yourself. They represent the threat that none of the other sacred prey do, save humanity itself. Its seeing the dangers of the Flesh maginified several fold, and seeing it in your own people.<br /> <br /> The Pure are good antagonists because they serve as one kind of mirror. The Bale Hounds serve as a mirror for the other extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:34:54-08:00","id":816134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=815952#post815952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good thoughts so far, thanks.<br /> <br /> To add another wrinkle to this discussion, what do Bale Hounds add that Idigam don't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I really like the Bale Hounds, I hope I can play, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To answer this question, I can sum it up in one word: <i>familiarity</i>. The Bale Hounds aren't an outside force that seeks to eradicate the Tribes of the Moon (or, to a lesser extent, the Pure). They can be anyone - your brother, your friend, your packmate. Think about any long-term friendship you've had. You know that person well - you can probably finish sentences for them. You've seen their triumphs, and, more pertinent to this discussion, you've seen their failures. A Bale Hound is like that - he's not from &quot;that pack down the street,&quot; he's <i>been in your pack for years</i>. He knows every pack member's foibles, their worries, and their fears. And when the time is right, he pulls the strings that keep the pack together. Tugs them as far as they'll go and beyond, until they snap, and the pack tears itself apart in blood and viscera.<br /> <br /> The idigam can't do that because no matter how much they study and plot and plan, they're still an outsider.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds are the most dangerous prey for one simple reason: <i>they're your friend.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:59:47-08:00","id":816146,"title":"","content":"That does make them a bit hard to implement, though. You really need to get a player on board for betraying everyone and possibly having their character killed by the other players. <br /> <br /> Not that it's not fun if you pull it off. I've actually done the double agent gig myself, albeit not in a Forsaken game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:11:28-08:00","id":816279,"title":"","content":"For the record, Bunyip's original post applies to me too. I do not quite get the love for the Bale Hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:39:40-08:00","id":816300,"title":"","content":"I am fond of the Bale Hounds for the same reasons I am fond of the demons of Inferno. Because they are close to the heart and their wickedness is very familiar, because they are emphatically humanized in their duplicity, flaws and selfishness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:13:59-08:00","id":816332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816279#post816279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, Bunyip's original post applies to me too. I do not quite get the love for the Bale Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div> I honestly think its mostly love of demons and possibly Black Spiral Dancers. But that's just me. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:32:57-08:00","id":816342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816332#post816332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I honestly think its mostly love of demons and possibly Black Spiral Dancers. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can assure you that, at least in my case, it's not love of Black Spiral Dancers. Demons...meh. (I prefer the Unchained in that category myself, but I'm a sucker for espionage stuff). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:47:51-08:00","id":816360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816146#post816146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does make them a bit hard to implement, though. You really need to get a player on board for betraying everyone and possibly having their character killed by the other players.<br /> <br /> Not that it's not fun if you pull it off. I've actually done the double agent gig myself, albeit not in a Forsaken game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you meant that the vision I expressed isn't easy to achieve. If that's the case, I might have focused too much on the &quot;Pack&quot;. It can be a player (we have done it and was awesome), but most of the time it will be an outsider that seems to be good. An ally that helps you fight a problem he himself created, just to get your trust. The guy that seems to be a victim, but in the end is the one pulling the strings.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds are the real boogie-man of stabilished and powerful Uratha. For them, everything else is predictable, even the might Indigam will fall to the powers of the Ithaeur and the common laws of Ban and Bane. The Pure will need to follow their Totems and behave in a certain way. Hosts are mindless most of the time, just a pest to be erradicated... But Bale Hounds are the guys you never really see comming. Also, the simple reason that players can turn into them make them worth having. Being a Pure isn't a temptation, it is just a matter of ideology. Bale Hounds add the possibility of selling your soul for power, and every game-line benefits from that possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:47:57-08:00","id":816361,"title":"","content":"As I was mentioned in OP, I'll take voice. I say openly \u2013 I\u2019m fanboy of Bale Hounds! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> They were most interesting antagonists to me in 1ED corebook \u2013 and now are equally intersting as Idigams, but from totally different reasons. In reality they are what I wanted from Black Spiral Dancers, but done much, <b>much</b> better. Here is quick list of this reasons:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Paranoia</b> \u2013 Everyone can be in the cult. Your packmate, your lover, your alpha \u2013 even your Tribes Elders. More than that \u2013 Bale Hounds are only one of two enemies that even Pure will help you get rid of. They are Outsiders that are Inside. And Hounds are best test of pack strength \u2013 if you survive one of you betraying you to the Maeljins, your new family will survive anything. But <i>do</i> you survive?</li> <li><b>Hell </b>\u2013 I\u2019m sucker for good \u201cdamned by Hell\u201d stories. <b>Inferno</b> is one of mine favorite general WoD supplements, I even won it\u2019s copy in our Polish contstest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mine typical <b>Hunter</b> stories are mix of <i>Exorcist</i> and <i>Supernatural </i>\u2013 so I\u2019m clearly fanboy of dark powers. But question is - <b>Why Hell is so much appeling to me?</b> It\u2019s because it\u2019s highlight how our own actions can lead to doom \u2013 and how Vices can be our undoing. Great gothic theme to explore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>\u201cHumanity\u201d </b>\u2013 By serving Lords of Sin, Bale Hounds are much closer to humans than most Uratha. When you look over Tribes \u2013 both Pure and Forsaken - and their philosophy \u2013 they are taking very much spirits stance. Weird Bans, hunting monsters or even other humans. Only veteran Bale Hounds will truly understand the Lust you feel to this pretty girl that do not even set eyes on you. Only Hound will arrange you to get this new shinny car and better job \u2013 you only need to give him three innocent children for next ritual. It is Evil, but it\u2019s Human Evil. I would also propose to let Bale Hounds choose third Anchor as Vice, after Blood and Bone. Or at least instead of Bone.</li> <li><b>History</b> - Bale Hounds adds interesting spin on historic events for the <b>Forsaken's</b> setting. It's written that Bale Hounds are large problem in mine &quot;home&quot; Europe, probably coming from the spread of Christianity leading to banning everything related to animism. When looking over this point, you can understand the Middle Ages werewolves that went by First Change in small communities. You were man becoming wolf, possessed by &quot;demon&quot;, seeing &quot;demons&quot; for half your life now ( as in Hisil ), calling &quot;monster&quot; by every story you know. Nothing surprising in the fact that many of Uratha might think that they are the Children of Satan and should lead the Hell on Earth.</li> <li><b>Silent Hill</b> - I love the game series and Wounds are to Shadow Realm, just like <a href=\"http://silenthill.wikia.com/wiki/Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Otherworld</a> is to Fog Silent Hill. If you want to appreciate much more the Wounds idea - just play those games or watch ( first ) movie. It's really scary and great stuff!</li> <li><b>Foes for the Tribes</b> - I also just realized that Bale Hounds will be greatest problem for Iron Masters, mine own favorites from Tribes of Moon, so it\u2019s also this on plus side. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-25-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:36:16-08:00","id":816396,"title":"","content":"Of course, you <i>could</i> have a game where <i>all</i> the players are secretly a bale hound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:38:27-08:00","id":816398,"title":"","content":"Wyrdhamster's point (<b>3</b>) about humanity seems the most interesting.<br /> <br /> I view werewolves as a mixture of crime story (like Narcos or The Shield), an animistic legend, and a nature documentary.<br /> <br /> Each one of those gets less and less tragic. Crime stories are mostly tragedies, which is great drama. The animistic legends are somewhat tragic, but more in the since of &quot;This is what we had to do&quot;, not &quot;This is where I went wrong&quot;. Nature documentaries can be sad, but I don't see most animals as having tragic natures.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds are all tragedy, and they represent great flaws and take power from the upswings of those tragic arcs and claim that the downsides were inevitable anyways. I see them taking the vice mechanic and narrative device and sewing through everything in the chronicle. Not only are they tragic, their enemies begin to take on tragic characteristics as well as they fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:45:10-08:00","id":816405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816332#post816332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I honestly think its mostly love of demons and possibly Black Spiral Dancers. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you know... it's the reasons people are saying?<br /> <br /> While the demon thing is clearly part of it (see wyrdhamster's post), I mentioned no such thing.<br /> <br /> Linking the Maeljin and demons shouldn't be off the table, but it should be one option (just like geists might be ghost-spirit hybrids) is one way to explain it, but it doesn't have to be explained officially in one fashion.<br /> <br /> The BSDs, to me, are more like the Pure in function. Only the most skilled BSDs can work around the Garou without being noticed as being a servant of the Wyrm. Most are simply going to be obvious enemies. They're less nuanced than the Pure, but they serve the same purpose as ideological enemies in direct opposition, not the role of the Bale Hounds as paranoia inspiring enemies that could be anyone you know. If anything, that was something Apocalypse simply lacked. Any of the Camps that would fill the same role as the Bale Hounds by going into the deep end in pursuit of whatever, hid themselves (often with the assistance of their Tribe to avoid public embarrassment as the Tribes tried to wipe out such dissidents themselves) to the point where most Garou would never know about them. It's hard to be paranoid about the Man-eaters, when few people outside the Bone Gnawers know they exist, and the majority of Bone Gnawers are fairly sure they killed off their cannibals. The Bale Hounds work as a constant rumor that everyone's heard stories of, but few know for sure if they've encounter them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":".  Weird error in original 01-25-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T15:24:17-08:00","id":816466,"title":"","content":"Apparently, people misunderstood the part where I said &quot;That's just me.&quot; As in, that's the main reason why <b><i><u>I</u></i></b> like them. I'm not speaking for anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T15:39:57-08:00","id":816477,"title":"","content":"Please don't get antagonistic with each other folks. Part of the purpose of this thread is seeing the different opinions. There's not much on Bale Hounds - around 32 pages of multiple options of what they could be. There's nothing concrete about Bale Hounds - a lot of people here seem to go with the idea of them as a tribe, but that's not definitive. <br /> <br /> Because Bale Hounds aren't definitive, I want to know the different opinions. Everyone's entitled to their own idea. <br /> <br /> So I'd please ask everyone to say what they think, and not take umbrage if someone's opinion is different from yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:03:44-08:00","id":816512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816466#post816466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, people misunderstood the part where I said &quot;That's just me.&quot; As in, that's the main reason why <b><i><u>I</u></i></b> like them. I'm not speaking for anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking for myself, I misunderstood the first sentence. To me, that read very much as, &quot;an observation of other people,&quot; not a statement of personal preference. As written, it felt far more like, &quot;here's what I think other people like about them from what I've seen,&quot; rather than, &quot;this is what I like.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:07:19-08:00","id":816515,"title":"","content":"Here is my answer to &quot;sell&quot; you:<br /> <br /> Werewolves with truly alternate belief systems and values.<br /> <br /> Bale hounds do not have the cookie cutter beliefs and/or values of other Uratha. Most Pure have strong ideological ties and as do most Forsaken as well. There is a reason bale hounds are detailed in the Blasphemies book. Bale hounds are outsiders and infiltrators to both groups. Their motivations tend to be much more personal and selfish than they are ideological indoctrination of the mainstream strange cult-like subcultures of Uratha. Werewolves go through a traumatic transformation that drives a wedge between them and their former lives, leaves them with instincts and emotions that rack their hearts, minds, and souls and preyed upon by groups social predators who brainwash these psychologically vulnerable with tribal rituals design to enforce conformity of thought and beliefs. The same may or may not be true of bale hounds but bale hounds have in some part broken free of those normative paradigm to more than a standard deviation from average, characteristically towards being more self-centered and self-serving than even the most selfish Pure or Forsaken. They are defined by vice and sins that color their worldview until it in a very real sense defines a major portion of who they are. These are not werewolves with flaws of moral characters, these are living flaws of moral character walking around wearing a husk of a supernatural predator that once was a mighty spiritual warrior fighting ideological battles for either balance or vengeance. Their sin has hollowed them out from the inside and now they can't even understand why what they do is wrong, nor would they care if they did; they are, depending on storyteller interpretation, past most chances of redemption, barring some epic saga or extreme contrivance of plot. They are the big bad wolves that brutally victimizes and violates the other wolves that thought they were big and bad, as if werewolf was a disturbing prison movie, just because they are nastier, meaner, and absolutely without qualm towards foul tactics. If other werewolves were to fight as dirty as bale hounds, they'd by definition <u>be</u> bale hounds.<br /> <br /> Also they bring morality themes into focus for the game with the most violence of any splat so far scheduled to be in the second edition. Geist: Sin-Eater gives werewolf a run for its money in the violence department due to dealing with death, frequently violent death, either your own or ghost's are central to that game. The hunt is a theme about primal savagery which can muddle morality themes. Bale hounds re-inject the theme of madness, sins and emotional damage caused by unspeakable acts and facing horrifying forces that is in the core Chronicles of Darkness back into the werewolf game by making it crystal clear that while even savage violence for ideological reasons can be normative justified within a society with the proper context, there are things which go too far and are not acceptable by anyone who is sane and/or moral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-29-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:23:50-08:00","id":816524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816477#post816477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing concrete about Bale Hounds - a lot of people here seem to go with the idea of them as a tribe, but that's not definitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they should lack the structure a tribe provides. Antagonistic tribes are already there in the form of the Pure. <i>Bale Hound</i> should just be a word you scream at the son of a bitch that that made your sister think suicide was a better option, and then took her soul and drank her blood as her body lay at the center of the ritualistic marked floor, all this to honor some nameless devil that made him so fucking powerful you will need to make every Pack around you, even the bastards who tortured you and almost ripped your Auspice out, that they need to unite and kill the him before he opens a gate to hell.<br /> <br /> At the same time, Hounds should have something that links them to each other. Maybe the Maeljin can offer some kind of power no other entity can. A new form? Freedom from the Werewolf condition? Mind control over other Uratha using the bones of the dead Ur-Farah? The ability to consume other Uratha to increase your own Primal Urge?<br /> <br /> I feel like Bale Hounds should be some kind of parasites that invisibly leech all the Tribes, slowly growing in power until they can rule their own Wounds, maybe becoming themselves new Malejin? Should the Maeljin be connected to the seven deadly sins? Spirits are already covering that. If Maeljin are alien even to the alien, what are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T18:12:15-08:00","id":816555,"title":"","content":"Watching this with great interest. I know next to nothing about Bale Hounds, aside from vague associations with Inferno, but I'm really digging how people are describing them (I love &quot;Sell Me On...&quot; threads).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:45:14-08:00","id":816601,"title":"","content":"My wife and child have been battling bouts of pneumoni\u00e6 and I've been particularly busy taking care of everyone and making sure they don't drive each other crazy. Otherwise I like to believe I'd have jumped on this thread sooner. I often find myself trying to explain things rather than sell them, I'm lousy at selling ideas, but the Bale Hounds are my favorites so here we go.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hounds offer opportunity to explore evil in its many forms. The antagonists of the other games, outside of Belial's Brood, really avoid a 'pure evil' label. They tend to have human aspects, and be sympathetic, or at the least understandable. Even the Pure, for all that some people hate them, are just on the other side of an argument about what's right and who's wrong. No one's really 'dedicated to evil,' but the Bale Hounds and the Brood.<br /> <br /> Through the Ninth Tribe, one of my favorite ideas, you get to explore what evil is when backed up by the powers of a werewolf. A Bale Hound of the Ninth Tribe is a demon incarnate, not bound by limits of ephemeral form or occult pacts and demonological stricture. These are the big bad wolves, the ones described in the write-ups of the various Maeljin in Blasphemies. They're corrupters, spreading their vice and indulging in it when they can and reveling in it. Big fan of Soulless Wolf, myself, and I have some headcanon based on some of the connections between his write-up and terms in Geist.<br /> <br /> The other big selling point is the pacts. These guys are the most common in the books, which says something considering how little 'text time' the Bale Hounds get. They're werewolves who wanted something, and were willing to make a deal to get it. Olivia Citysmith wanted to enact a grand plan, Feng Shui'ing her city of Chicago to maximize its Essence potential, and made a deal with a Maeljin to live long enough to do it. Adelita Sundancer saw the enemies of her people all around, and knew they were going to lose, and that loss would mean death. She didn't want to be a part of that, so she found a Maeltinet and made a deal to survive. 'She fell to darkness not out of hate but out of pragmatism and fear.' Moriarty of the Black Moon eXtreme found himself bleeding to death, his quest to wipe out the vampires of Denver doomed to never get off its feet, when he was offered a deal to become something other than roadkill. These are the more 'human' werewolves. The People make mistakes, the People can be weak, the People are hungry for something, power, renown, love. The Maeljin can give it to them. These Bale Hounds can be anyone. They don't have to be ravening psychopaths or cold-blooded killers, they're just someone who wanted something more and were corrupted by price they paid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:45:51-08:00","id":816603,"title":"","content":"I never liked Bale Hounds, I always felt that the niche they inhabit is already filled with Pure and Ghost Wolves. I see them as a bit of a relic from older edition, those are W:tF Black Spiral Dancers influenced by 1ed Vampire: the Requiem VII. Compared to other Forsaken enemies, they seem nearly comical and like the concept was beaten to death long, long time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:53:27-08:00","id":816612,"title":"","content":"In my one and only Forsaken chronicle so far one of the earliest antagonists I introduced was a Bale Hound. I introduced him as a respected elder in the greater Forsaken community who was supportive of this new pack, even had one player take dots in Mentor with him filling the role. They talked to him, sought advice from him, really had a chance to get to know him, even as they hunted the mysterious individual messing with the wound in their region. When they finally fought him he had a face and a name. On the other hand Randal 'Runs to Ground', the Pure hunter who harassed them in their own territory, tracking them, luring them into ambushes, summoning spirits to raid their locus and even fire bombing their 'Den' while they were in it...Randal really pissed them off and they took greater pleasure (and showed no mercy) in ripping his head off, but he was still just a faceless threat who only had a name because he had a reputation. In the end he was just another Boss Battle, one of many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T22:43:02-08:00","id":816682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816603#post816603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked Bale Hounds, I always felt that the niche they inhabit is already filled with Pure and Ghost Wolves. I see them as a bit of a relic from older edition, those are W:tF Black Spiral Dancers influenced by 1ed Vampire: the Requiem VII. Compared to other Forsaken enemies, they seem nearly comical and like the concept was beaten to death long, long time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept of werewolves was beaten to death too, but we got a nice refreshing update that breathed life back into the line and there are a number of people that want to see Bale Hounds get the same refresh. Pure and Ghost Wolves don't fill the niche the Bale Hounds did, not in any way, shape or form, nor are they comical. If that's how they were presented to you then the person doing the presenting was handling them incorrectly.<br /> <br /> If you don't like them that's fine, people have different tastes, that's why we're asking for an add on supplement that impacts the base game in no meaningful way. That's the advantage of the metaplot free toolbox setup of CoD, no need to include supplemental material you don't want.<br /> <br /> I also have to point out that the thread is &quot;[Sell me on] The Bale Hounds&quot; not Tell Me Why You Don't Like Them&quot;. That's called threadcrapping around here, don't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-26-2016, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T23:34:56-08:00","id":816702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816477#post816477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's nothing concrete about Bale Hounds - a lot of people here seem to go with the idea of them as a tribe, but that's not definitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to run Bale Hounds are <i>secret</i> Tribe - they infiltrated both Tribes of Moon and Pure, follow Soulless Wolf and doing they own plans - But they all are also members of normal Tribes, worming they way in to positions of power in Uratha society. That way they, someday, can tip the balance and uncover Bale Hounds in full glory, just before them bringing literal Hell on Earth ( and Shadow ).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about few failed instances of this plan when this could be historical events - maybe times of Inquisition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T04:54:29-08:00","id":816782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Miriander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816603#post816603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked Bale Hounds, I always felt that the niche they inhabit is already filled with Pure and Ghost Wolves. I see them as a bit of a relic from older edition, those are W:tF Black Spiral Dancers influenced by 1ed Vampire: the Requiem VII. Compared to other Forsaken enemies, they seem nearly comical and like the concept was beaten to death long, long time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not easy to do a demonic splat and not have them come off as comedic EVULZ. However, it is possible. It all comes down to how its run. Just take a look at the Seers and Belial's Brood books. Both are roughly analogous to Bale Hounds, and they're done in a fairly believable fashion that's actually fairly attractive in a game.<br /> <br /> Another thing you have to keep in mind is that the concept of what a Bale Hound is and does has kind of evolved with the release of books. One of which was Blasphemies, and another of which was Inferno. And they're going to change again with the shift of focus away from universal Vices / sins in 2e. There's no such thing as universal evil in the CofD anymore. At least, that's not the impression I have (unless you count the Abyss). So, while there's still a place for the Bale Hounds, its one that simply cannot fit the same cartoon evil you suggest.<br /> <br /> Of course, my personal problem with the Bale Hounds is figuring out what I'm going to do with them when I remove the Inferno from my 2e cityscape. I've redesigned my game to only include vamps, wolves, mages, 'lings, and mortal-GMC. I can fill the humanistic corruptor roll with werewolves, but I feel like, without that Infernal crossover feeling, there's just something missing from the Hounds.<br /> <br /> So, while they don't fit every game, I do think there's room for them in a lot of games, which is all that matters, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:15:42-08:00","id":816793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816782#post816782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, my personal problem with the Bale Hounds is figuring out what I'm going to do with them when I remove the Inferno from my 2e cityscape. I've redesigned my game to only include vamps, wolves, mages, 'lings, and mortal-GMC. I can fill the humanistic corruptor roll with werewolves, but I feel like, without that Infernal crossover feeling, there's just something missing from the Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>See <b>Silent Hill</b> - it's almost perfect representation of Shadow Realm and Wounds. And you do not need the <b>Inferno</b> stuff, per se in there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's just really wicked and alien - but also weirdly human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:26:46-08:00","id":816799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816793#post816793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See <b>Silent Hill</b> - it's almost perfect representation of Shadow Realm and Wounds. And you do not need the <b>Inferno</b> stuff, per se in there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's just really wicked and alien - but also weirdly human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Meh, that's more of a mage-thing. It is a crossover setting, so the overlap feels forced. Doesn't fit at all with what I've got in mind for the cityscape. Plus, this is set in Vegas. Silent Hill doesn't fit in Vegas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T22:20:09-08:00","id":817413,"title":"","content":"Since we do have real world mythology of werewolves being humans cursed by infernal powers I think one can use the Bale Hounds to model that myth. They aren't &quot;true&quot; werewolves, but rather something the Maeljin have created in mockery of the things that tend to inhibit the production of wounds in the Shadow. Something that can get into the werewolves' world and act as saboteurs. Something that can win the trust of &quot;real&quot; werewolves and turn them to the Maeljins' use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T22:33:32-08:00","id":817419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=816682#post816682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have to point out that the thread is &quot;[Sell me on] The Bale Hounds&quot; not Tell Me Why You Don't Like Them&quot;. That's called threadcrapping around here, don't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Quite. I have my own set of doubts, I don't much need others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T23:44:12-08:00","id":817436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817413#post817413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we do have real world mythology of werewolves being humans cursed by infernal powers I think one can use the Bale Hounds to model that myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have Lycon'Ur cursed by Zeus in Wroc\u0142aw setting, that is embodiment of Gluttony...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T07:42:37-08:00","id":817585,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds were a relatively major part of my longest Werewolf Chronicle back in 1e.<br /> <br /> They came in three flavours.<br /> <br /> The first was the PCs mentors. The campaign began when a savage Pure attack wiped out the older half of the pack, the NPCs who had been looking after the fledgling werewolf PCs. These NPCs had become Bale Hounds due to the influence of an insane Lune who had been corrupted by Baalphegor. She had convinced the pack that they had to 'fight fire with fire' and turn to darker paths in order to help keep an ancient horror under the city restrained; she'd been set to this task ages ago but had been tainted by it as the centuries turned. The Bale Hounds kept their activities secret, but as the PCs began to dig into the pack's history they slowly uncovered various discrepancies and weird elements of what had been going on. The Pure had targeted the pack because of a particular totem that had discovered the Lune's nature. In the end, the PCs discovered that a particularly tricksy Bale Hound loose in the city, one with amazing capabilities of concealment and masking, was actually the NPC Irraka from the pack who had escaped the purge.<br /> <br /> <br /> The road to the end here involved the Lune getting free again and, before the PCs eventually discovered her corrupted nature, she managed to convince two pack members to start down the same dark path that led to the earlier generation becoming Bale Hounds. Fortunately they discovered the truth soon enough before she convinced them to do the REALLY horrific stuff for power. In the end, the mad Lune went down insane and fighting, still convinced SHE was the good one following Luna's orders and that the Lunes that were being sent to take her out were the REAL betrayers. The Bale Hound Irraka met his end down the scope of the Iron Master sniper when he attempted to protect his mistress, finally forced out of the shadows and into combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second were the Baalphegori Bale Hounds at work attempting to release the horror under the city, the Devouring Spiral - a spirit-god that had been killed but was too powerful to actually die, once a spirit called Echoes of the Past who represented learning from history but who had been warped by the Maeljin into a horrifying abcess wedged part way into the Underworld. These Baalphegori were manipulating the cannibal-cult of 10,000 Leaves, collecting parts of the hostile timeline's pages and using the cultists as sacrifices and meals full of hunger-Essence. They attempted to free the Devouring Spiral but mostly got stamped out and rooted out by the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Finally was Spirals of Bright Agony, an antagonist who, if I remember, actually died well before the Chronicle began but still had a major impact on it. He was the insane, genius Bale Hound of Psuelak who had terrorised the city a generation ago, whose schemes were still unwinding and causing havoc, and who was the cause of the most powerful Forsaken in the area having been exiled from the city and hence unable to intervene much in what was going on. Pseulak had its own plans for the Devouring Spiral, and it was Spirals of Bright Agony who had orchestrated those plans. The PCs kept encountering the legacy of his actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So for me Bale Hounds work as the Enemy Within, the Corruption, and the Uncertainty. Bale Hounds cause mistrust; they leave schemes that must be unravelled and unpicked; and they provide horrible werewolf cults that can follow different ethos and mythos to the Forsaken and the Pure. Now, in 2e, I rather like to push the latter part away from the Bale Hounds alone; my games now feature bizarre heretic or blasphemous cults that would have been Bale Hounds in 1e but don't actually have anything to do with the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> In fact, I rather like the idea of broadening Bale Hounds out as a concept on precisely that basis - all the heretics and blasphemers and weird, unrelated cults and mythos all under the same heading as far as Pure and Forsaken are concerned. Some are the classic Bale Hounds following the Maeljin, but so are any number of witch-cults, totemic vessels of gibbering alien abominations and the like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:22:20-08:00","id":817622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817585#post817585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I rather like the idea of broadening Bale Hounds out as a concept on precisely that basis - all the heretics and blasphemers and weird, unrelated cults and mythos all under the same heading as far as Pure and Forsaken are concerned. Some are the classic Bale Hounds following the Maeljin, but so are any number of witch-cults, totemic vessels of gibbering alien abominations and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm okay with that. I like that a lot. It reminds me of how 2e's Banishers were broadened (or that's how it seems to be)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:31:49-08:00","id":817635,"title":"","content":"^ The heretical nameless orders of forsaken, if you would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:40:41-08:00","id":817644,"title":"","content":"I absolutely support the idea of broadening the concept of Bale Hounds to encompass a variety of nasty werewolves with nasty agendas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:40:28-08:00","id":817697,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds are people. A Bale Hound is every werewolf, on a bad day. <br /> <br /> You don't join the Bale Hounds by approaching the gods of sin and asking to join up, you join them by being yourself - on a bad day. <br /> <br /> Your grandfather dies. There's grief and there's shock, but there's also rage, rage at the doctors who botched the surgery that should have been a very easy operation, who didn't take the necessary precautions. <br /> <br /> The new girl gets the promotion that you have been promised. It's probably simply because she's more attractive than you. <br /> <br /> Your wife has stopped sleeping with you. She simply doesn't find you attractive any more. She's probably sleeping around. <br /> <br /> Doesn't that make you angry? Doesn't that make you feel wronged? Shouldn't someone pay? <br /> <br /> Add to this the emotional, deeply passionate nature of the Forsaken race. We all have felt really, really angry at one point or another in our lives. When werewolves feel angry, they don't feel like hitting someone the way we do, they feel like transforming into 3 meters of raging wolf-death, tearing someone's throat out and drowning him in his own blood. <br /> <br /> The Bale Hound philosophy isn't scary because it's about alienation from humanity or worship of Outer Evil, it's scary because it's about human emotion, human vice, and human feelings gone wrong. What makes the Bale Hounds tragic, sympathetic figures is that their horror is human horror.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:51:52-08:00","id":817713,"title":"","content":"To be fair, and in that line of thought, as there's humans who are more cruelly-inclined, there's likely werewolves who are too, without requiring them to have a bad day. After their First Change they find themselves in a pack, probably the time they've been closest to other people, and they still can't get someone to understand their need to hurt, to ruin others and their deep fulfillment at seeing others suffering. They get patronizing pats on the shoulder in return, told they'll get over it, as other packmates figure it's just a vestige of Basu-Im or some spirit Influence and not their true self.<br /> <br /> So they see something in the Maeltinet, something that calls out to a part of them that their pack will never understand, a hunger that Luna and all the following of Father Wolf's path doesn't satisfy.<br /> <br /> And that's when Soulless Wolf makes its offer and they find a place to belong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:10:48-08:00","id":817723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817585#post817585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I rather like the idea of broadening Bale Hounds out as a concept on precisely that basis - all the heretics and blasphemers and weird, unrelated cults and mythos all under the same heading as far as Pure and Forsaken are concerned. Some are the classic Bale Hounds following the Maeljin, but so are any number of witch-cults, totemic vessels of gibbering alien abominations and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's precisely how I would like them portrayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:23:13-08:00","id":817734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817585#post817585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I rather like the idea of broadening Bale Hounds out as a concept on precisely that basis - all the heretics and blasphemers and weird, unrelated cults and mythos all under the same heading as far as Pure and Forsaken are concerned. Some are the classic Bale Hounds following the Maeljin, but so are any number of witch-cults, totemic vessels of gibbering alien abominations and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather see the line between Forsaken and Pure and Bale Hounds blurred altogether; so that you get to have all sorts of packs and cults and a myriad of different set of beliefs, that are somewhere between points of extremes represented by Forsaken/Pure/Bale Hound dogma.<br /> <br /> I.e. &quot;this pack over there has rejected the Moon and kills anyone who gets close to their territory. Those crazy fuckers over there are still on the Moon path but they think all werewolves are actual demons straight out of Christian mythology. And there's the crazy survivalists in the east who have helped us out every now and then; but they still worship very strange spirit gods, so don't talk religion with them.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game is more interesting to me, if, once you meet a new pack, you can't immediately attach a label like &quot;Forsaken&quot; or &quot;Pure&quot; and deal with them accordingly. Diversity is fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:25:56-08:00","id":817737,"title":"","content":"(Put differently - I think that the Forsaken should have their share of weird blasphemers and heretics and diverse, strange cults as well. I think, once you get into that sort of thing, the label &quot;Forsaken&quot; and &quot;Pure&quot; and &quot;Bale Hounds&quot; start getting blurry, and it's more reasonable to consider each individual pack as a faction of its own; which is precisely how I like things.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:40:52-08:00","id":817756,"title":"","content":"The Bale Hounds write up in Blasphemies actually mentions that there are Bale Hounds who don't realize they are Bale Hounds, they're acting out of self interest which ends up promoting the interests of a particular Maeljin. I like the idea of the corrupted not actually realizing they are corrupt, but hey, politics is a hobby of mine. It's not as difficult to corrupt the ideologically pure as one would think. It's rather easy if one knows what they are doing, and the Maeljin most certainly know what they are doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":".  typo correction. 01-27-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:11:30-08:00","id":817776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817734#post817734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd rather see the line between Forsaken and Pure and Bale Hounds blurred altogether; so that you get to have all sorts of packs and cults and a myriad of different set of beliefs, that are somewhere between points of extremes represented by Forsaken/Pure/Bale Hound dogma.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've undertaken an approach along those lines but from a different angle, which should be a bit more evident when The Pack comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:38:12-08:00","id":817789,"title":"","content":"You already get that to a degree. Forsaken doesn't mean good, Pure bad. A group of hard core environmentalists might be Hunters in Darkness as much as Predator Kings, and any Bone Shadow, or religious person-turned-werewolf could become a Fire-Touched. Lineages of werewolves are likely to have traditions that make them seem like Ivory Claws, there was one in the fiction anthology where, I think, the werewolf was from a long line of Blood Talons and sort of upset his family when he sought an outside pack to join. And as Darksider has pointed out, anyone can further the cause of the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> Our first werewolf game, the Pure book hadn't come out, and since the book didn't mention it we didn't play them with bright red glowing scars instead of silvery markings. When it was revealed to us that the Pure had infiltrated the city we were in, it was sort of like a game of spy, where you couldn't tell who was who, and then when you did you had to make sure they thought you were on the right side. A Bale Hound was taking advantage of all of this to unite the Pure in the guise of a rather renowned werewolf he had killed.<br /> <br /> In our current game, my character is basically a Bale Hound, with a personal totem that's tasked him with various corruptions, but is more mechanically a member of the Iron Masters, as we decided it would be easier and more in-tune with the game to just run with that than homebrew something up.<br /> <br /> While in the setting I've run, unfortunately never Forsaken, there was a quartet of Bale Hounds who caused trouble in the city. I think I've mentioned this before, but Raker runs a cult of Pride out of a research department, and uses her influence to have wolf-blooded institutionalized so that she can perform experiments on them, no one ever ran into her, I think because they were a bit genre savvy and knew to avoid the mental hospital, but she was mostly a background antagonist for the hunter games. Vaylor was a great white hunter who went through the First Change well towards the end of his life, after joining the Bale Hounds he organized the local Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club, sending them out on hunts that would bring the Pure and Forsaken population to war and destroy the hunter community. He was a very active antagonist, and I find it amusing so many of us have used the Bale Hounds in mentor roles. The last, Angel, mostly went into our vampire story, as a servant of the 'Selfish Three' idea I found neat in Blasphemies, worshiping Mammon, Carnala and Baalphegor, his cult was really poorly organized and mostly made up of people who wanted things badly enough to do bad for it. He had been captured and imprisoned by the Forsaken after his theft of the eye of one of the Secondborn, but the eye was lost and he refused to tell them where it was. After much pleading the Secondborn agreed not to wreck the town providing the werewolves did not stop searching until they found it. When Vaylor's plan went through, there were no werewolves to search and the countdown to destruction began. Though Angel's story mostly unfolded in a vampire game and the eye had fallen into the hands of vampires who were using it for their own gain, unaware of the larger threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:03:21-08:00","id":817809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817585#post817585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I rather like the idea of broadening Bale Hounds out as a concept on precisely that basis - all the heretics and blasphemers and weird, unrelated cults and mythos all under the same heading as far as Pure and Forsaken are concerned. Some are the classic Bale Hounds following the Maeljin, but so are any number of witch-cults, totemic vessels of gibbering alien abominations and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew those Ghost Wolves in Wroc\u0142aw were Bale Hounds in disguise! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:52:20-08:00","id":817857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817776#post817776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've undertaken an approach along those lines but from a different angle, which should be a bit more evident when The Pack comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:54:12-08:00","id":817862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817789#post817789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You already get that to a degree. Forsaken doesn't mean good, Pure bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all what I mean. I didn't say anything about good or bad. I don't want the lines to be drawn along that axis. I want werewolves to be <i>diverse </i>in their belief. <br /> <br /> Stuff like the Lodge of the Grotto, or the Lodge of the Feast, or the Feral werewolves in the Territories sourcebook, or the pretty strange lodges in Blasphemies. That sort of thing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:02:52-08:00","id":817882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817585#post817585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, I rather like the idea of broadening Bale Hounds out as a concept on precisely that basis - all the heretics and blasphemers and weird, unrelated cults and mythos all under the same heading as far as Pure and Forsaken are concerned. Some are the classic Bale Hounds following the Maeljin, but so are any number of witch-cults, totemic vessels of gibbering alien abominations and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Nameless Orders for Werewolves, but with more stigma?<br /> <br /> I could get behind writing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:07:58-08:00","id":817943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817862#post817862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all what I mean. I didn't say anything about good or bad. I don't want the lines to be drawn along that axis. I want werewolves to be <i>diverse </i>in their belief.<br /> <br /> Stuff like the Lodge of the Grotto, or the Lodge of the Feast, or the Feral werewolves in the Territories sourcebook, or the pretty strange lodges in Blasphemies. That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apologies, I understood what you meant, I just thought good/bad was an easy example, especially considering its where most go to in regards to the Pure/Forsaken. But I do think the book has already done a lot to go in that direction. Various aspects of the Oath are taken more or less seriously depending on the pack or individual, just a glance at the settings section shows you a wide variety of beliefs among the example werewolves, and we've already seen that the Pure aren't as mindlessly antagonistic toward the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing Lodges will go the way of Shadow Gifts, so outside of certain Lodges with a heavy fundamentalist slant, more Lodges that accept werewolves of all creeds. Just a guess, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:56:18-08:00","id":818021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=817622#post817622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It reminds me of how 2e's Banishers were broadened (or that's how it seems to be)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, where did you see that? I haven't seen anything yet about 2e Banishers and it's something I'm wanting to use in my chronicle, so I'd appreciate it if you've got a link or anything I can look at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:07:39-08:00","id":818105,"title":"","content":"While they still fit a sort of 'Hunters that are Mages' role, they're not all Timori or whatever the Legacy was. Somewhere in the depths of all the <b>Mage</b> previews, comments, and forum spoilers is the idea that some are like Timori but others are simply Mages who use Integrity rather than Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Arc finished my thought by mentioning the Nameless Orders, and even the Lower Depths fit that re-imagining of Bale Hounds: &quot;These are the things that we dont' like to talk about so we'll lump them all together in one category&quot; or so someone in-character would say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:56:35-08:00","id":818712,"title":"","content":"I tend to think about antagonists through ideological lenses; everyone covered a lot of the 'role in a story' and vibe kind of material well, but I want to revisit ideology and emphasize what Bale Hounds represent to me: <b>surrender</b>.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has moved more and more to emphasizing the first purpose of a werewolf as hunting and not fighting, but the underlying ideological tension is the same: how you approach your impossible duty and try to live up to it. Pure might twist that duty to serve the interests of the Shadow and their own rabid ideology, but they care about duty - depending on how you interpret them they might be more relaxed about their non-genocidal duties or make poor choices of priority, but they're still living up to their duty in their own way.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds say fuck that, <b>I hate losing, I'm joining the side that wins in the end</b>.<br /> <br /> They give up their duty, surrender to the opposition, and make a deal. There's a lot of resonance to that being a surrender to old-school vices, and I think it fits better with 2E's take on vice than people give it credit for, but I don't think it really needs to be anything other than what you're supposed to not do. To paraphrase, and forgive me for this - werewolves either die fighting or live long enough to find themselves becoming a Bale Hound. They're incredibly understandable, because they're what every werewolf could be if they stopped fighting the world and gave in and joined up.<br /> <br /> To project forward into the 2E paradigm, though, I think it's also important to think about what they hunt. Whether they're a tribe or not, they should have a specific kind of prey - maybe it's what their masters point them at, maybe it varies interestingly by Maeljin/Patron and trying to act out a vice on the hunt - and I think that however it works or varies, on some level their hunts are fundamentally <i>selfish</i>.<br /> <br /> Final point here: ideologically speaking, I think you want to compare them as much to the Seers as to the Scelesti. They're sellouts for power and respite and their own desires. You should always be able to place a Bale Hound in the context of who they're working for. You don't have a rat without the cops, you don't have Cypher without Agent Smith and the machines. Etc.<br /> <br /> ...that rambled, and I don't have time to concise-ify it, but I have feelings about the Bale Hounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:51:58-08:00","id":818755,"title":"","content":"My one and only Bale Hound, while there was something selfish he hoped to gain, surrendered to the inevitable. The pitch he threw at the players was that the world was going to Hell in a handbasket, the Maejlin are going to win but we can help decide which one comes out on top. He had thrown his lot in with Gluttony, arguing that it would only eat 1/3rd of the population (I was basing the Maejlin on Persian myth) where as Wrath would lay waste to everything.<br /> \u200bI used my Bale Hound as a mentor because that is how I see them working, they are wolves in sheep's clothing (pun intended), the enemy hiding within, undermining and poisoning werewolf society. They are enemies with similar strengths that don't automatically get a 'kill' response like orcs meeting elves in Tolkien. This allows them to interact with the players before the killing starts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T22:11:39-08:00","id":818997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=818712#post818712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To project forward into the 2E paradigm, though, I think it's also important to think about what they hunt. Whether they're a tribe or not, they should have a specific kind of prey - maybe it's what their masters point them at, maybe it varies interestingly by Maeljin/Patron and trying to act out a vice on the hunt - and I think that however it works or varies, on some level their hunts are fundamentally <i>selfish</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bale Hounds have as Sacred Prey the same as their original Tribe - i.e. Gauntlet related things, like spirits, humans or Hosts, for Forsaken, or ideological for Pure. <b>The thing is I envision that Bale Hounds maybe &quot;Hunt&quot; by finding and coming to terms with them</b> - your Hunter in Darkness Bale Hound can can find Beshilu nest, go in to middle of it - only to &quot;talk over&quot; the local avatar of Plague King that his Maeljins masters will help them the Nest if they take out his enemies.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds still Hunt - they just do not need to kill their prey at the end of it. Interesting then would be what does make Predators Kings Bale Hounds - What, they let humans live only to disrespect the Hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T23:00:45-08:00","id":819014,"title":"","content":"No Uratha ever *has to* end a hunt with a kill. I can see what you're saying, but the killing part is redundant, and the rest will just lead to failed Siskur-Dah for the pack, which they will notice. Therefore I don't think this is a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T23:36:06-08:00","id":819023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819014#post819014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Uratha ever *has to* end a hunt with a kill. I can see what you're saying, but the killing part is redundant, and the rest will just lead to failed Siskur-Dah for the pack, which they will notice. Therefore I don't think this is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Failed Siskur-Dah? You assume that Bale Hound will just go and talk Hosts in front of normal pack - and it's <i>wrong</i> assumption for this scenario.<br /> <br /> What I have in mind was that <i>if</i> Bale Hound works inside normal pack, he goes on secret meeting <b>without his packmates</b>, in &quot;free time&quot;. Infiltration work only if you doing it, you know, <b>in secret</b>.<br /> <br /> Here are ideas what various Tribes heresies as Bale Hounds could do:<ul><li><b>Blood Talons</b> - Hunting normal Uratha, serial killer style, leading to conflict inside Forsaken and Pure</li> <li><b>Bone Shadows</b> - Spreading Wounds and Maeljin corruption in spirits</li> <li><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - Using Hosts for personal reasons, shaping Gauntlet by using them, giving heads up about coming Hunts</li> <li><b>Iron Masters</b> - Running mortal cults of Maeljins</li> <li><b>Storm Lords</b> - Spreading Claimed of the Maelinet?</li> <li><b>Fire Touched</b> - Analogical to Bone Shadows?</li> <li><b>Ivory Claws</b> - Mixing of bloodlines? I would proposed werewolves spirits children, if they would be still in 2ED.</li> <li><b>Predator Kings</b> - Making Prey more sturdier in Hunt, to prolong it?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T00:55:55-08:00","id":819041,"title":"","content":"Working for the Maeljin would require fulfilling the needs of that particular entity. If I was redesigning the Maeljin to work with Forsaken I'd have each Maeljin favor corrupting a particular tribe (9 Maeljin, one for each of the 8 Tribes plus Ghost Wolves). Some associations are easier to make than others, some need a little more mental effort to make the association. Here's an example list off the top of my head. Pride, Sloth, Wrath, and Violence seem pretty solid to me, the others might need to be shifted around a bit.<br /> <br /> Wrath=Blood Talons<br /> Lust=Iron Masters<br /> Pride=Storm Lords<br /> Envy=Ghost Wolves<br /> Greed=Ivory Claws<br /> Gluttony=Bone Shadows<br /> Sloth=Hunters In Darkness<br /> Deceit=Fire Touched<br /> Violence=Predator Kings<br /> <br /> So a Bale Hound from a particular Tribe would probably, but not always, serve the interests of the Maeljin that favors corrupting their particular Tribe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T02:06:45-08:00","id":819052,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea on 9 Maeljin connected to 9 Tribes. I do not sure with Lust for Iron Masters, but most is spot on. I would probably go more with Iron Masters as Greed, but Ivory Claws Lust sounds weird. Maybe Claws as Envy and Ghost Wolves as Envy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819041#post819041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrath=Blood Talons<br /> (...)<br /> Violence=Predator Kings</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most biggest problem I have with this interpretation - <b><i>What</i> is real difference between those two?</b> In the end you have both bloody soaked wolves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-29-2016, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T02:16:48-08:00","id":819057,"title":"","content":"Wrath is a spiritual thing, violence is a material thing. One is internal, the other external.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T02:46:38-08:00","id":819071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819023#post819023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Failed Siskur-Dah? You assume that Bale Hound will just go and talk Hosts in front of normal pack - and it's <i>wrong</i> assumption for this scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't assume that. Have I given you cause to believe that I would take the most implausible interpretation, that the pack would be stupid enough to just sit there and watch while the Bale Hound does some 'secret deal' with the prey. Wyrd, I give you the benefit of the doubt that you propose ideas in good faith, I'd ask that you return the favour and don't assume that when my opinion is that I don't agree with your idea, it's not because I've taken the dumbest interpretation possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819023#post819023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I have in mind was that <i>if</i> Bale Hound works inside normal pack, he goes on secret meeting <b>without his packmates</b>, in &quot;free time&quot;. Infiltration work only if you doing it, you know, <b>in secret</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the pack's Siskur-Dahs fail. And they start investigating. And they work out why. And the Bale Hound dies.<br /> <br /> I don't agree that this particular idea is a good one. I do appreciate that you are proposing ideas for discussion here.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T02:48:02-08:00","id":819072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819041#post819041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Working for the Maeljin would require fulfilling the needs of that particular entity. If I was redesigning the Maeljin to work with Forsaken I'd have each Maeljin favor corrupting a particular tribe (9 Maeljin, one for each of the 8 Tribes plus Ghost Wolves). Some associations are easier to make than others, some need a little more mental effort to make the association. Here's an example list off the top of my head. Pride, Sloth, Wrath, and Violence seem pretty solid to me, the others might need to be shifted around a bit.<br /> <br /> Wrath=Blood Talons<br /> Lust=Iron Masters<br /> Pride=Storm Lords<br /> Envy=Ghost Wolves<br /> Greed=Ivory Claws<br /> Gluttony=Bone Shadows<br /> Sloth=Hunters In Darkness<br /> Deceit=Fire Touched<br /> Violence=Predator Kings<br /> <br /> So a Bale Hound from a particular Tribe would probably, but not always, serve the interests of the Maeljin that favors corrupting their particular Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is an idea that has more merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T03:02:57-08:00","id":819077,"title":"","content":"Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:09:32-08:00","id":819159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819052#post819052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is the most biggest problem I have with this interpretation - <b><i>What</i> is real difference between those two?</b> In the end you have both bloody soaked wolves...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Darksider, but we're talking about Thurifuge, so I'll emerge from the shadows and throw my two cents<br /> <br /> The connection between them works not because of the end result but because of the reason those wolves went out looking for blood in the first place. While both tribes are the most &quot;warrior badasses&quot; of their respective side, there's a slight difference in attitude that makes the more vulnerable to a Maeljin rather than the other (we're talking in broad strokes, naturally)<br /> <br /> For Asmodai, blood is a natural consequence of wrath, but the point is not blood. It's reacting destructively to every bump on your road and take every perceived slight as a dire insult. Under Wrath, you hurt people because your blood runs hot-red and you don't even consider another approach to your problems. Wrath burns, it takes your thoughts away. In the warrior culture of the Blood Talons, it's far too easy to fall for that.<br /> <br /> Violence is different. Yes, when blood is spilled and people are hurt it empowers Thurifuge no matter what (it's part of the reason because he's so strong), but violence can be cold. Wrath might lead to violence, but Thurifuge also feeds on violence made for the sake of violence. The reasoned, planned, &quot;now we go out and hurt them not because they wronged us but because it feels good&quot; kind of thing. It's violence pursued in a exercise of power and superiority, done for the simple reason that you can. That brings us to the Predator Kings. They're warriors like the Blood Talons but the specific identity of their warrior ideal has a different focus, wherein violence is as much as glorified as strength. You're a predator, after all. Hurting prey is what you do. It's when this sort of grotesque sacred duty becomes more a personal pleasure than a holy crusade, when, pardon the pun, it loses its purity, that Thurifuge comes knocking<br /> <br /> Or at least that's how I see it. Darksider's reasoning might have been different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-29-2016, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:36:39-08:00","id":819179,"title":"","content":"I think second edition has changed the '9 Maeljin' idea.<br /> <br /> But in first edition, Blasphemies covers the difference pretty well.<br /> <br /> On Wraith, 'Rather than deny their primal anger as a separate part of themselves with no ties to their reasoning minds, the Hounds of Wrath accept the fury as sacred and valuable in all aspects of thought. They see it as part of the human as well as the beast; they gorge on anger and indulge in the rush. The Forsaken fear their anger and release it when the time is right. The Bale Hounds feed their anger and unleash it when the opportunity is ripe. Release is one thing, and unleashing quite another.'<br /> <br /> And on Violence, 'To the Hounds of Violence, the very act of inflicting pain and suffering is sacred. Rather than hurt their enemies in the heated rage of true wrath, Thurifuge\u2019s Hounds commit their sins in cold blood, and with obsessive, psychotic forethought. The act of violence itself feeds their Maeljin totem, and any fury or passion before the deed is just wasted energy.'<br /> <br /> Though in regards with linking them to a specific tribe, I'd like to point this out, about Dire Wolf of the Predator Kings. 'Oldest and most ruthless of the spirit wolves, Dire Wolf was Urfarah\u2019s savage nobility given form. But what appeared as wisdom and temperance was often tainted with spite, for Huzuruth \u2014 utmost predator among predators \u2014 is one of the few Firstborn touched with true malice. It is the malice of a creature that knows its own power and fears nothing. The malice eats into his very being, souring his great wisdom and tainting all who bond with him.'<br /> <br /> My preference is that Bale Hounds are on a hunt for evil. To draw it out in others, in the land around them. To make spirits Maeljin-corrupt, to have other Uratha and vampires and supernaturals and humans 'give in.' The lazier can go after the weak and wounded, while the more fierce go after the pious and willful. Outside of the Hounds of Sloth, the Maeljin need life, so the hunt not requiring a kill to end it is good for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:29:36-08:00","id":819273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819159#post819159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Asmodai, blood is a natural consequence of wrath, but the point is not blood. It's reacting destructively to every bump on your road and take every perceived slight as a dire insult. Under Wrath, you hurt people because your blood runs hot-red and you don't even consider another approach to your problems. Wrath burns, it takes your thoughts away. In the warrior culture of the Blood Talons, it's far too easy to fall for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like something you'd expect more of a tribe of savages that won't abide human invention in their territory because &quot;it insults the natural order of things&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819159#post819159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Violence is different. Yes, when blood is spilled and people are hurt it empowers Thurifuge no matter what (it's part of the reason because he's so strong), but violence can be cold. Wrath might lead to violence, but Thurifuge also feeds on violence made for the sake of violence. The reasoned, planned, &quot;now we go out and hurt them not because they wronged us but because it feels good&quot; kind of thing. It's violence pursued in a exercise of power and superiority, done for the simple reason that you can. That brings us to the Predator Kings. They're warriors like the Blood Talons but the specific identity of their warrior ideal has a different focus, wherein violence is as much as glorified as strength. You're a predator, after all. Hurting prey is what you do. It's when this sort of grotesque sacred duty becomes more a personal pleasure than a holy crusade, when, pardon the pun, it loses its purity, that Thurifuge comes knocking.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not violence. The violence that Therifuge eats on is the planned conflicts. He's literally the Architect of Violence. Think D-Day. Think Hiroshima and Nagasaki. The Blood Talons, on the other hand, are the tribe that most resemble those ideas and concepts, because they are nearly universally organized in military fashion.<br /> <br /> Therifuge feeds when every soldier is a cog in the machine. Asmodai feeds when it's personal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:52:58-08:00","id":819297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819273#post819273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like something you'd expect more of a tribe of savages that won't abide human invention in their territory because &quot;it insults the natural order of things&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally see it under a different light, with the targets of Predator Kings' hate suffering for opposing to their rules and worldviews on a matter of principle, with the reaction as violent as it is because they are the savages they are. Still, it's definitely a matter of shades, so I won't declare myself the &quot;one who has it right&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819273#post819273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not violence. The violence that Therifuge eats on is the planned conflicts. He's literally the Architect of Violence. Think D-Day. Think Hiroshima and Nagasaki. The Blood Talons, on the other hand, are the tribe that most resemble those ideas and concepts, because they are nearly universally organized in military fashion.<br /> <br /> Therifuge feeds when every soldier is a cog in the machine. Asmodai feeds when it's personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might have been not clear, and for this I apologize, but that's sort of my point as well. Thurifuge is exactly that: cold, impersonal, violence. I don't know, I see more potential for that in the dogmatic crusade of the Pure, with its emphasis on seeing the others as the <b>&quot;</b>Enemy&quot; rather in the military organization of the Blood Talons. We're speaking relatively here, there's plenty of potential for both the Maeljin in those two Tribes but, if I were to pick one, I'd associate Thurifuge more with the Predator Kings than others","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:05:47-08:00","id":819345,"title":"","content":"Thurifuge feeds on all types of violence, mindless or planned. Asmodai feeds on excessive anger, which usually leads to violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:28:11-08:00","id":819463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819345#post819345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thurifuge feeds on all types of violence, mindless or planned. Asmodai feeds on excessive anger, which usually leads to violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Not all of them. There's justifiable violence, the violence a predator inflicts on it's prey, cruel as it may be, it's not personal. It's unavoidable. Otherwise the world would be a hell-hole with Thurifuge ruling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:54:17-08:00","id":819486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819463#post819463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Not all of them. There's justifiable violence, the violence a predator inflicts on it's prey, cruel as it may be, it's not personal. It's unavoidable. Otherwise the world would be a hell-hole with Thurifuge ruling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to feed on those, too, just not as much.<br /> <br /> 'Thurifuge is a powerful totem \u2014 perhaps even the most powerful of all the Maeljin, purely because of his primary Influence. Violence is the cause of most of the world\u2019s Wounds splitting open in the Shadow, and the importance of this \u2014 the very resonance of this Maeljin\u2019s power \u2014 cannot be overstated. While any Maeljin\u2019s Influence can bleed into the spirit wilds, the sheer amount of war and battle that rage across the human and animal worlds means that Wounds fuelled by violence are undisputedly the most common.'<br /> <br /> It's also called out for having the most allies, as violence spirits are pretty much everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:56:15-08:00","id":819488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819486#post819486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems to feed on those, too, just not as much.<br /> <br /> 'Thurifuge is a powerful totem \u2014 perhaps even the most powerful of all the Maeljin, purely because of his primary Influence. Violence is the cause of most of the world\u2019s Wounds splitting open in the Shadow, and the importance of this \u2014 the very resonance of this Maeljin\u2019s power \u2014 cannot be overstated. While any Maeljin\u2019s Influence can bleed into the spirit wilds, the sheer amount of war and battle that rage across the human and animal worlds means that Wounds fuelled by violence are undisputedly the most common.'<br /> <br /> It's also called out for having the most allies, as violence spirits are pretty much everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E, Thurifuge is strong. First-among-equals strong","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T14:01:23-08:00","id":819492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819488#post819488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1E, Thurifuge is strong. First-among-equals strong</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets the nicest palace, too, in the First Wound and on top of, or perhaps even carved from Father Wolf's bones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T14:31:24-08:00","id":819507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819492#post819492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It gets the nicest palace, too, in the First Wound and on top of, or perhaps even carved from Father Wolf's bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always liked that bit. It's from Lore of the Forsaken, right? I hope that, even if things change in the Second Edition, they'll still do something with Father Wolf's grave and/or bones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T14:33:22-08:00","id":819508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819463#post819463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Not all of them. There's justifiable violence, the violence a predator inflicts on it's prey, cruel as it may be, it's not personal. It's unavoidable. Otherwise the world would be a hell-hole with Thurifuge ruling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, all of them. It is not restricted to just planned violence as you stated earlier. You don't think a drunk slapping around his wife feeds Thurifuge? A bully picking on a target of opportunity doesn't feed him? A predator's violence is still brutal but it's usually quick, so that wouldn't offer much of a meal, which is why Thurifuge was the weakest of the Maeljin during the time of Pangaea according to the lore. Get that predator to go on a prolonged killing spree however, that gets his attention. He'd love you to think that justified violence doesn't feed him. That's how he recruits unwitting Bale Hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-29-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T14:35:45-08:00","id":819510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819507#post819507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always liked that bit. It's from Lore of the Forsaken, right? I hope that, even if things change in the Second Edition, they'll still do something with Father Wolf's grave and/or bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Maeljin all got little write-ups there, the Blasphemies write-ups focus more on what the Bale Hound servants of the individual Maeljin are like. They're all pretty neat but the palace bit really rubs the whole death of Father Wolf thing in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T15:24:36-08:00","id":819535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He'd love you to think that justified violence doesn't feed him. That's how he recruits unwitting Bale Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you are saying, and I feel the sentiment behind your words. I would very much like to agree with you as well, in all sincerity and without any sarcasm. Unfortunately, while valuing peace is wonderful, it also can be a path to sin, and that sin is sloth. Sloth does not act, it lets others act and takes risks for it for it. Several virtues are fed by actions that could be deemed violent, such as Justice and Fortitude. Fortitude goes by several other names and one of names is Courage. Sin selfishly harms others, risks harm to others, and/or ignores truths; virtues are self-risking for the sake of moral principles or others as defined within 1e World of Darkness. Predators are not wrathful, all violence is not wrath, and sometimes violence can indeed even be virtuous.<br /> <br /> Saying all violence is evil is simplistic doesn't reflect the complexities in the reality of the real life or that of the Chronicles of Darkness. It borders on hyperbole meant to short-circuit reason with false compassion. There is nothing compassionate about refusing to defend the weak and helpless from abusers or self-righteously brush that duty towards action to those less afraid of violence.<br /> <br /> The deepening of pacivity of western culture seems a trend that is more about the domesticating of obedient helpless workers than civilizing of civic-minded educated critical thinkers.<br /> <br /> All that being said, I absolutely love what you said and it has the potential to be a real source of conflict within the game and sparks meaningful examination of how morally questionable each use of violence is. It raises doubts in the justification behind actions and as such makes a great story. It is my hope you like my point of view for the story opportunities it presents if it were held by characters in game, even though you may or may not agree with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-29-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T15:48:44-08:00","id":819544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819508#post819508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He'd love you to think that justified violence doesn't feed him. That's how he recruits unwitting Bale Hounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that this is strictly speaking correct. I agree with Pale Crusader's points above, but I also wanted to bring up something from one of the other books.<br /> <br /> If he were a spirit of violence, then this would be true, spirits aren't fussy and feed off of any manifestation of their concept. That's just how spirits work and there's no moral dynamic to it. However in <i>Inferno</i> it suggests that demonic spirits (which is implied to <b><i>maybe</i></b> include the Maeljin) possess both a spiritual concept and a vice-based &quot;key&quot; which unlocks it. Thus you could have a spirit of Fire, whereas you'd have a demon that feeds off of Fires that were set out of Greed. This makes it harder for them to feed on essence, but the added complexity also allows them to think in more complex fashions than a normal spirit could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":".  Fixing a typo. 01-29-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T15:52:57-08:00","id":819546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819535#post819535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying all violence is evil is simplistic doesn't reflect the complexities in the reality of the real life or that of the Chronicles of Darkness. It borders on hyperbole meant to short-circuit reason with false compassion. There is nothing compassionate about refusing to defend the weak and helpless from abusers or self-righteously brush that duty towards action to those less afraid of violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, while all violence isn't evil, and violence being evil is not a thing World of Darkness suggests, Thurifuge is. And Thurifuge gains off of all violence, because it's a spirit of violence. It's why a hospital spirit, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\">such as Acrozatarim's</a>, can be a menacing and predatory thing.<br /> <br /> From Lore of the Forsaken, regarding Thurifuge, 'The Maeljin feeds on the spiritual resonance of every act of violence that has occurred since the dawn of time, and many Ithaeur with a twisted interest in the Maeljin have said that Thurifuge stands on the cusp of becoming a Celestine.'<br /> <br /> A Celestine, mind, is of the rank of Luna or Helios. At least in first edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819544#post819544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However in <i>Inferno</i> it suggests that demonic spirits (which is implied to <b><i>maybe</i></b> include the Maeljin) possess both a spiritual concept and a vice-based &quot;key&quot; which unlocks it. Thus you could have a spirit of Fire, whereas you'd have a demon that feeds off of Fires that were set out of Greed. This makes it harder for them to feed on essence, but the added complexity also allows them to think in more complex fashions than a normal spirit could.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same section, however, it also says this.<br /> <br /> 'As one of the examples shows, some powerful demons have multiple Malapraxes. They could have many Vices bound to a single Key, many Keys for a single Vice or a combination of both. Demonologies speculate that some Archdemons rule every Vice linked to a particular Key, or every Key linked to a specific Vice. Thus, Mammon is the lord of all Greed, and Pazuzu reigns over every evil act that utilizes, or is committed during a storm.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-29-2016, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:03:55-08:00","id":819553,"title":"","content":"Exactly, Nofather. I 'm not just applying personal preference to my interpretation. I'm going by info from the three different books that address the Maeljin. Lore of the Forsaken, Blasphemies and Inferno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:19:05-08:00","id":819568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819546#post819546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'As one of the examples shows, some powerful demons have multiple Malapraxes. They could have many Vices bound to a single Key, many Keys for a single Vice or a combination of both. Demonologies speculate that some Archdemons rule every Vice linked to a particular Key, or every Key linked to a specific Vice. Thus, Mammon is the lord of all Greed, and Pazuzu reigns over every evil act that utilizes, or is committed during a storm.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually forgot about that part (and thankyou for remembering the term Malapraxes, I was wracking my brain for that one). However, you can see how frequently vice comes up in connection with the Malapraxes. Regardless of how broad an archdemon's mandate might be, I don't think it's intended to include any neutral or benevolent manifestations of their spiritual phenomenon. <br /> <br /> So for example I don't think Thurifuge would gain power from... say, a hawk swooping down and grabbing a rabbit which is purely an act of nature and doesn't touch on vice in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:22:23-08:00","id":819570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819486#post819486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems to feed on those, too, just not as much.<br /> <br /> 'Thurifuge is a powerful totem \u2014 perhaps even the most powerful of all the Maeljin, purely because of his primary Influence. Violence is the cause of most of the world\u2019s Wounds splitting open in the Shadow, and the importance of this \u2014 the very resonance of this Maeljin\u2019s power \u2014 cannot be overstated. While any Maeljin\u2019s Influence can bleed into the spirit wilds, the sheer amount of war and battle that rage across the human and animal worlds means that Wounds fuelled by violence are undisputedly the most common.'<br /> <br /> It's also called out for having the most allies, as violence spirits are pretty much everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read your quote. War, Battles, carnage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:39:36-08:00","id":819580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819570#post819570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read your quote. War, Battles, carnage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we really have to play the quote game? Because there's more:<br /> <br /> &quot;While any Maeljin\u2019s Influence can bleed into the spirit wilds, the sheer amount of war and battle that rage across the human and animal worlds means that Wounds fuelled by violence are undisputedly the most common. <b>Of course, it isn\u2019t just war</b> \u2014 look at any situation in which humans cluster together. Most urban crimes involve an element of violence, and this resonates across into the Earth\u2019s reflection. The alley where someone was raped, the bar where someone was shot and killed, even the road outside a club where fights break out all the time at the weekends. Every wife-beating, terrorist strike, every act of war \u2014 all feed Thurifuge just as they Wound the Shadow&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Maeljin feeds on the spiritual resonance of <b>every</b> act of violence that has occurred since the dawn of time...&quot;<br /> <br /> War is there, obviously, but so is domestic violence and brawls. It's not about being a Thurifuge fanboy, people. Its how things are written, in a way that gives not much space to interpretation. 1E Thurifuge was huge, there's no way around it. He's the one who gets the shiniest stuff and his Bale Hounds are the only ones with a sidebar made specifically for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-29-2016, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T17:05:53-08:00","id":819588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819546#post819546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, while all violence isn't evil, and violence being evil is not a thing World of Darkness suggests, Thurifuge is. And Thurifuge gains off of all violence, because it's a spirit of violence. .'</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree that violence spirits can eat violence essence and can sustain itself in the presence of violence. Thurifuge isn't just any violence spirit though, it is more complex than that. It is a Sin, Wrath, Cruelty, Carnage, War, and Atrocity Spirit just as much if not more than it is a Violence Spirit. All those are in harmony with the resonance and nature of Thurifuge. Self-risking violence done with restrain, due compassionate consideration towards those it is acted upon done for unselfish and righteous reasons would be drastically out of sync with the harmony of the vast majority concepts/essences/resonances that makeup Thurifuge, and from my understanding of spirit ecology would begin to change Thurifuge if it allowed itself to consume or absorb enough without mitigation towards its core self with the appropriate feeding.<br /> <br /> It might be possible cruel wicked violence to consume selfless righteous violence, in the same way sorrow can conceptually consume happiness and happiness can conceptually consume sorrow. In that case I'd be wrong, but then that would mean a great enough force of brave righteous justice violence spirits could be the best hope of getting rid of Thurifuge by devouring it.(or a large enough peace spirit)<br /> <br /> Gathering that force of selfless brave justice violence spirits would be exceedingly difficult when evil violence forces seek to devour and pollute them, but makes an Epic Apocalyptic chronicle idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T17:44:27-08:00","id":819609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819588#post819588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-risking violence done with restrain, due compassionate consideration towards those it is acted upon done for unselfish and righteous reasons would be drastically out of sync with the harmony of the vast majority concepts/essences/resonances that makeup Thurifuge, and from my understanding of spirit ecology would begin to change Thurifuge if it allowed itself to consume or absorb enough without mitigation towards its core self with the appropriate feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's entirely possible for it to change attitudes, if everyone in the world decided to only do 'good violence,' but until then it is the Architect of Violence, and whether good violence or bad violence or accidental, providing it's violence, it's feeding Thurifuge. Wrath is the domain of another Maeljin, Asmodai, sin alone doesn't feed Thurifuge, either does cruelty, which doesn't have to involve violence. But if its violence, it is within the domain of Thurifuge.<br /> <br /> You're right that Thurifuge isn't just any violence spirit, it seems to be the top violence spirit, the reflection of all violence that ever was. <br /> <br /> Something like Carnala, though, the Lady of Lust, has a much narrower profile. 'Carnala is the Incarna of all shallow loves, of all the worthless, degrading sex in the world, of all the filthy passion that turns violent and abusive - of all the desiring affection that ever turns impure.' She isn't empowered by animals rutting or missionary sex between a married couple in the dark solely for the purposes of procreation. Thurifuge is more powerful because he has a broader profile, and gains more resonance from a wider variety of acts.<br /> <br /> It's all very interesting, personally. One of the thories is that the Maeljin were once normal spirits, corrupted by sin. But it's entirely possible they were always Something Else. Just as it's possible that they are some remnant of Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-29-2016, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T06:32:13-08:00","id":819786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819609#post819609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's all very interesting, personally. One of the thories is that the Maeljin were once normal spirits, corrupted by sin. But it's entirely possible they were always Something Else. Just as it's possible that they are some remnant of Pangaea.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in the second edition, Vices are not the 7 main Sins anymore, at least not by the rules. Everything that is selfish is now considered a vice. Maybe that's the reason they are different? Some connection with the deep selfishness of Humanity, something that can't be expressed by anything else in the Universe, since only humans have consciousness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T12:34:56-08:00","id":819920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=819786#post819786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in the second edition, Vices are not the 7 main Sins anymore, at least not by the rules. Everything that is selfish is now considered a vice. Maybe that's the reason they are different? Some connection with the deep selfishness of Humanity, something that can't be expressed by anything else in the Universe, since only humans have consciousness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nine, there were nine Maeljin, and they weren't restricted by humanity's belief in the Seven Sins or what you could put in the Vice line on your character sheet then and I doubt they will be now. But it's far too early to say what's exactly going to happen with them second edition, it hasn't appeared in anything but a small sidebar which may just reconfirm the same 9 Maeljin, or offer a thousand more.<br /> <br /> What we've been quoting has been from first edition books. Since there's no second edition information regarding the Maeljin, this should be obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-30-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T14:11:37-08:00","id":835361,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say a quick thank you to everyone who participated in this thread. You've certainly given me food for thought about the appeal of Bale Hounds, and their place in 2nd ed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T19:42:06-08:00","id":835528,"title":"","content":"I'm sure others have said what they like, and its certainly going to be similar to my opinion, but I'm going to voice it all the same without digging through 7 pages of forum posts (mostly time constraints).<br /> <br /> I LOVE the enemy within. The ability to play the back stabber, to keep THAT secret from the rest of the pack requires a great deal of acting, subterfuge, not just on the table but off as well. Your players and companions cannot know, else wise they will start lookig for a way to find it in game. It's an alluring power.<br /> <br /> Then we get into the cultural aspects of them. I love soulless wolf, and his ritual of eating sins. A bit pointless now with 2nd edition harmony change, but its very evocotive all the same. Their portrayal in blasphemies is like a less edgy spirals. If Forsaken are akin to heavy metal then the bale hounds are akin to doom metal. Its the rythm of burning churches and destroying civilization. The aspect in all people that twinges at the idea of anarchy, at freeing the beast. True they're servants in worse ways then the pure, but damn do they win.<br /> <br /> Hell looking at the first edition tainted moon gift list.... It was bleak and savage without being unnecessary. The black spirals are so steeped in rape, not just of the flesh but of the spirit. The bale hounds more feel like the guy who sold his soul for insane powers, and still got to come out on top. At that point it isn't about being the under dog. Once you make your move you're beyond being touched. Your former pack is dead. You now have an insane home field advantage for any invading pack (if you did your job right), and if you've recruited more bale hounds (assuming its the 9th tribe motif and not the multiple sins motif) then you have an unstoppable force from spiritual hell. <br /> <br /> It's an allure that appeals to anyone who loved Al Pacino in the devil's advocate. It's that cultural break that goth kids looks for. Its that black metal you love in your early 20's. You were a monster as a forsaken, true, but as a Bale Hound? You can become a god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:19:11-08:00","id":837767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=835528#post835528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an allure that appeals to anyone who loved Al Pacino in the devil's advocate. It's that cultural break that goth kids looks for. Its that black metal you love in your early 20's. You were a monster as a forsaken, true, but as a Bale Hound? You can become a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>... then the twist?<br /> <br /> All this temptation, betrayal, power with a price. It's all wonderful stuff. 110% support it and the stories that come forth from it.<br /> <br /> The last laugh though, should be had by the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bale Hounds get the perks as long as they keep paying. Vices, torments schemes, bad mojo plans. They keep doing them, the power keeps flowing. Prices slowly (sharply?) increase as tend to happen with evil incarnate. If they keep paying them they're still in good graces.<br /> <br /> When though, the line is drawn, and the Bale Hound or Hounds say, 'okay, it's been fun, please stop the ride now.' The Maeljin say 'no.'<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now you Chronicle of Darkness writers are a brilliant bunch, but what I would love to see in addition to all of this torment, temptation, double-agents of evil deal for Bale Hounds in 2e is what happens when the tables get turned on them. When the Maeljin laughs, its last laugh.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds should not just be the horror of the Self, the Other Within, that's the start. The real horror? The aftermath of winning. The true price of power. The Spiritual and Fleshy dissemination of a Bale Hound. Is it a crazy predator wolf? A mewling husk? A new form or shape? The loss of control, of purpose, of self?<br /> <br /> Power corrupts, absolute power corrupts absolutely. Corrupting others might stave off their own damnation, but what awaits a Bale Hound really at the end?<br /> <br /> That's what I want to find out in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T14:26:49-08:00","id":837771,"title":"","content":"Hopefully they'll expand upon the 'end game' theorized in first edition.<br /> <br /> A Bale Hound who has done well becomes a Maeladar. An immortal demon-spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T15:27:26-08:00","id":837797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/815913-sell-me-on-the-bale-hounds?p=837771#post837771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully they'll expand upon the 'end game' theorized in first edition.<br /> <br /> A Bale Hound who has done well becomes a Maeladar. An immortal demon-spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Bale Hounds who haven't done well?<br /> <br /> Presumably there are a lot more of these then those who have. Those who have made a quick bargain, a desperate one, or who thinks themselves a master of manipulation, but in truth is lacking. Few things mark a Bale Hound, if they became one out of bad choices, convenience or practicality rather than devotion, when they hit that limit where they don't play the Maeljin's game or serve.<br /> <br /> What then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:50:08-08:00","id":840771,"title":"","content":"When a bale hound fails they are usually eliminated by the forsaken. Somethjng happened where they got caught and that's usually how it goes. <br /> <br /> If they fail in their duties then soulless wolf eats them. I believe it's mentioned in blasphemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:03:32-08:00","id":840782,"title":"","content":"He seemed interesting in the fiction. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There is a Bale Hound who has called upon him to eat their sins, having just killed the rest of their pack. What they don't know is that one of the pack has survived and is playing dead. Before he leaves, Soulless Wolf warns the Bale Hound that she left one alive, and she 'earned this warning' because of her offering. The icing on the cake was the line just before that, when the hiding werewolf hears Viruhk-Ur speaking with the Bale Hound, not knowing what they're talking about and hoping the spirit wasn't telling her that he was hiding.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Presumably once you've sworn yourself to them, failure forfeits your soul or something. I wouldn't be adverse to deepening the system, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}